flags-cflags: define ARM for arm builds with clang

HotSpot's arm sources require the ARM macro; without it the generated
ad_arm.cpp stops the build:

  ad_arm.cpp:19921:4: error: "ARM must be defined"

FLAGS_SETUP_CFLAGS_CPU_DEP only adds -DARM in its gcc branch, so every
clang-built arm target (all of ours -- the NDK is clang) misses it. Add it to
the clang branch too. Guarded by FLAGS_CPU = arm, so nothing else is affected.

Equivalent to termux-packages openjdk-25 patch 0030 (Henrik Grimler); ours
appends to CFLAGS_CPU_JVM rather than overwriting it.

diff --git a/make/autoconf/flags-cflags.m4 b/make/autoconf/flags-cflags.m4
index a2fbae9..9efcb32 100644
--- a/make/autoconf/flags-cflags.m4
+++ b/make/autoconf/flags-cflags.m4
@@ -759,6 +759,12 @@ AC_DEFUN([FLAGS_SETUP_CFLAGS_CPU_DEP],
     fi
 
   elif test "x$TOOLCHAIN_TYPE" = xclang; then
+    if test "x$FLAGS_CPU" = xarm; then
+      # HotSpot's arm sources require ARM to be defined; without it
+      # ad_arm.cpp fails with #error "ARM must be defined". The gcc
+      # branch above already does this, clang needs it too.
+      $1_CFLAGS_CPU_JVM="${$1_CFLAGS_CPU_JVM} -DARM"
+    fi
     if test "x$FLAGS_OS" = xlinux; then
       # ppc test not really needed for clang
       if test "x$FLAGS_CPU_ARCH" != xarm &&  test "x$FLAGS_CPU_ARCH" != xppc; then
